```mermaid
%% Sequence Diagram: Search by Image (CBIR)
%% Based on Chapter 7 — Detailed Design

sequenceDiagram
    actor Customer
    participant StoreSPA as Store SPA<br/>(Vue 3)
    participant Carter as Carter Endpoint<br/>(SearchByImage.Endpoint)
    participant Handler as SearchByImage<br/>QueryHandler
    participant Embedding as Embedding Sidecar<br/>(Python / FastAPI / Fashion-CLIP)
    participant Db as ApplicationDbContext<br/>(EF Core + pgvector)
    participant Cache as HybridCache<br/>(L1 Memory / L2 Redis)

    Customer->>StoreSPA: Upload fashion image
    StoreSPA->>Carter: POST /api/catalog/storefront/search-by-image<br/>multipart/form-data
    Carter->>Handler: sender.Send(new Query(imageBytes))

    Handler->>Cache: TryGet(cacheKey: imageHash)
    alt Cache hit
        Cache-->>Handler: Cached results
    else Cache miss
        Handler->>Embedding: POST /embeddings<br/>{image: base64}
        Embedding->>Embedding: Preprocess<br/>(resize 224x224, normalize)
        Embedding->>Embedding: Fashion-CLIP inference<br/>(torch → 512-d vector)
        Embedding-->>Handler: {embedding: [0.0123, -0.0456, ...]}

        Handler->>Db: SELECT vi.*, v.sku, p.name<br/>FROM variant_images vi<br/>JOIN variants v ON ...<br/>JOIN products p ON ...<br/>ORDER BY vi.embedding <=> @embedding<br/>LIMIT 20
        Db-->>Handler: Top-K similar images

        Handler->>Cache: Set(cacheKey, results, 5min)
    end

    Handler-->>Carter: Result<PagedResult<SearchResult>>
    Carter-->>StoreSPA: 200 OK<br/>{products: [...], similarityScores: [...]}
```

## Diagram Description

This sequence illustrates the **Content-Based Image Retrieval (CBIR)** flow, a key thesis contribution. Design decisions:

1. **HybridCache for embedding results** — repeated searches for the same image (e.g., user refreshes) avoid re-computing the embedding.
2. **Cosine similarity (`<=>`)** — pgvector operator optimized for normalized Fashion-CLIP vectors.
3. **LIMIT 20** — Top-K retrieval with a fixed cutoff for predictable response times.
4. **JOIN chain** — variant_images → variants → products to return full product context, not just image records.

**Evidence**: `ImageEmbedding.Inference.cs:21-36`, `Vector.Configuration.cs`, `ApiTests/Catalog/Storefront/search-by-image.http`
